  "title": "Business World Model",
  "summary": "This paper introduces the concept and architecture of a Business World Model (BWM), a world model specialized for business and organizational environments. We propose a business-semantics-centric formulation in which states, dynamics, and feasible actions are linked to business entities, their attributes, and their relationships. Within this framework, intelligent agents can simulate alternative action sequences, estimate their effects on future business outcomes, and evaluate trade-offs under uncertainty and business constraints. A churn case study of a media subscription business demonstrates that the system recommends options meeting the churn-reduction target within the revenue constraint.",
